{
  "title": "Olecranon Stress Fracture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3127/olecranon-stress-fracture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 5 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Olecranon Stress Fractures are rare elbow injuries that predominately affects throwing athletes.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can usually be made with plain radiographs of the elbow but may require an MRI or CT scan to confirm the diagnosis in the early stages.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally rest from pitching, pain control, and brief period of immobilization.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "predominantly involves the **epiphyseal plate**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fractures line may propagate to be either transverse or oblique in orientation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "three commonly accepted theories",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**olecranon posteriomedial impingement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**triceps traction force**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**valgus extension overload**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated injuries with throwing movements",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ulnar collateral ligament tears",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "medial epicondyle avulsion fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**posteromedial olecranon pain of the throwing arm**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "improves with rest",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "worse with throwing movements",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mild swelling over olecranon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "localized tenderness",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**valgus instability stress test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may indicate associated UCL injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3127/images/screen_shot_2014-07-30_at_9.31.03_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP, lateral, oblique views of elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "optional views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**valgus stress views**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**contralateral elbow for comparison**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "physeal widening, delayed fusion, or fragmentation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "widening of the medial joint space with UCL injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3127/images/screen_shot_2014-07-30_at_9.29.26_pm.jpg",
              "caption": "olecranon stress fracture"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "best seen on lateral views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**typical fracture pattern**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "originates from the articular surface",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "runs toward the dorsal-proximal direction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**suspected UCL tear**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "coronal T2 fat-saturated views",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "T-sign indicative of UCL tears",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3127/images/a520fdd3202e1f_13-ucl-tear-2.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "short-term administration of NSAIDS, rest +/- temporary splinting",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first-line treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "modalities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "initial 4-6 weeks of rest (removal from sport for up to 3 months)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "progressive ROM exercises",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "avoiding valgus loading forces (e.g. throwing)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "electrical bone stimulation may also be considered",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "consider vitamin D and calcium supplementation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open internal fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "delayed fracture union",
                      "table": null,
